Subject:   Cloud Computing
Experiment No: 3
Title:  Hosting a Web Server on AWS EC2

Aim:Install a web server (Apache or Nginx), and host a sample webpage accessible over the internet.
Theory:
Amazon EC2 provides resizable compute capacity in the cloud. Students will learn about instance types, key pairs
Procedure:

1.Log in to the AWS Management Console.

2.Navigate to EC2 → Launch Instance.

3.Select Ubuntu (Free Tier) AMI and a t2.micro instance type.

4.Create/Select a Key Pair and Security Group (allow SSH/HTTP).

5.Launch the instance.

Connect via SSH
ssh -i key.pem ubuntu@<public-ip>

Conclusion:A running EC2 instance
